#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:3
msgid "Pandoc Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:10
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:12
msgid ""
"The pandoc path is ****parse with pandoc, then apply snapper**** — not "
"“guess markdown lines like the built-in parsers.”"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:14
msgid "Pandoc reads the file (any format it supports) into its document AST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:16
msgid ""
"Snapper walks that AST and reflows only prose-bearing nodes (``Para`` / "
"``Plain``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:18
msgid ""
"Nodes pandoc already classified as structure (``Header``, ``CodeBlock``, "
"``Table``, …) are left alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:20
msgid ""
"The mutated AST is written through an in-process FFI writer when the loaded "
"library exports one, otherwise ``pandoc -f json --wrap=preserve``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:22
msgid "This is not a splice of the original bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:24
msgid ""
"That is how snapper can format everything pandoc can read (typst, asciidoc, "
"docx, html, …) without inventing per-format line heuristics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:26
msgid "How to run step 1 (same step-2 walker):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:28
msgid ""
"**Auto** — ``--pandoc-backend auto`` (default): prefer in-process FFI when "
"``libsnapper_pandoc`` loads, else CLI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:30
msgid ""
"This amortizes the GHC RTS for **parse**. The shipped library is reader-"
"only, so the writer still needs ``pandoc`` on ``PATH`` unless that library "
"exports a writer (no silent spawn)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:33
msgid ""
"**CLI** — ``--pandoc-backend cli``: ``pandoc -t json`` (full reader set of "
"the installed binary)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:35
msgid "Explicit error if ``pandoc`` is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:37
msgid ""
"**FFI** — ``--pandoc-backend ffi``: require ``libsnapper_pandoc`` (explicit "
"error if missing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:39
msgid ""
"Writer still needs ``pandoc`` on ``PATH`` when the library has no writer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:44
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:46
msgid ""
"****CLI backend.**** Pandoc 2.x or 3.x on ``PATH``. The CLI default uses "
"pandoc when an FFI writer or ``pandoc`` on ``PATH`` is available. Otherwise "
"it keeps the native line parsers (no error, no silent all-prose). With ``--"
"use-pandoc``, a missing or failing pandoc is an explicit error (no silent "
"all-prose). Pass ``--native`` to force today's line parsers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:53
msgid ""
"****Writer.**** The library ``libsnapper_pandoc`` is reader-only. The write "
"step still needs ``pandoc`` on ``PATH`` (help and errors say so). A library "
"that exports ``snapper_pandoc_write`` stays in-process for write too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:58
msgid ""
"****FFI backend (dynamic).**** Build ``native/snapper-pandoc``, set "
"``SNAPPER_PANDOC_LIB`` to ``libsnapper_pandoc.so`` (or put it on the search "
"path). A missing library with ``--pandoc-backend ffi`` errors with ``pandoc "
"FFI library unavailable`` (fail-closed; never silent all-prose)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:62
msgid ""
"****FFI backend (co-linked / one binary).**** Feature ``pandoc-colink`` is a "
"**build** path: produce ``libsnapper_pandoc.a`` with ``native/snapper-pandoc/"
"build-static.sh`` (``ghc -staticlib``), then Cargo absorbs that archive into "
"a single ``snapper`` executable (``--gc-sections``). No "
"``SNAPPER_PANDOC_LIB`` discovery and no multi-hundred-MB ``libHS*`` RUNPATH "
"graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:73
msgid "See ``native/snapper-pandoc/README.md``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:78
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:92
msgid ""
"The CLI default uses pandoc (auto FFI, then CLI) when an in-process writer "
"or ``pandoc`` on ``PATH`` is available. Otherwise it keeps the native line "
"parsers (no error, no silent all-prose). Pass ``--native`` to force today's "
"line parsers. Pass ``--use-pandoc`` to require the pandoc path (explicit "
"error if FFI and ``pandoc`` are missing). The writer still needs ``pandoc`` "
"on ``PATH`` unless the library exports a writer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:98
msgid ""
"****Speed.**** Warm in-process FFI parse is a few times native cost; a cold "
"``pandoc`` CLI process reloads the GHC RTS (tens of ms). The writer is that "
"CLI spawn unless the FFI library exports a writer — it is never a surprise. "
"Snapper also caches pandoc JSON ASTs by content hash (memory + disk under "
"``$XDG_CACHE_HOME/snapper/pandoc-ast``). Re-formatting the same source skips "
"pandoc parse. Disable with ``SNAPPER_PANDOC_CACHE=0``; override dir with "
"``SNAPPER_PANDOC_CACHE_DIR``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:108
msgid "When to use pandoc vs built-in parsers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:110
msgid ""
"****Pandoc**** (CLI default when available): structure from pandoc’s model "
"and coverage of formats without a built-in parser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:112
msgid ""
"****Built-in**** (``--native``): fast, source-oriented parsers for Org / "
"LaTeX / Markdown / RST (e.g. full ATX lines as structure)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:114
msgid ""
"The two paths are different pipelines, not two ways to fake the same source "
"lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:119
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:121
msgid ""
"Pandoc's reader deletes comments (RST ``..`` comments, HTML comments) and "
"therefore ``snapper:off`` / ``snapper:on``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:123
msgid ""
"``--use-pandoc`` shields RST ``..`` comments and ``snapper:off`` / "
"``snapper:on`` so the written output still contains that text and exits 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:125
msgid ""
"Other HTML / Org / LaTeX comments that are not snapper pragmas may still be "
"dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:127
msgid ""
"Round-trip is through the AST (not a perfect source-preserving rewrite of "
"every markup character)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:129
msgid "FFI library is optional; wasm/editor bundles do not embed GHC/pandoc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/howto/pandoc-backend.rst:131
msgid ""
"CLI pandoc versus editor native is the contract: the CLI default may use "
"pandoc; VS Code, Obsidian, Word, wasm, and LSP stay on native parsers."
msgstr ""
